  "body": "[PR1128](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1128) leaves six rank-seven helper candidates at the fixed PR589 D/A/scatter cut. This contribution tests an explicit early-restoration mechanism: five candidates lose a required target dependency even at their least first restoration frame; helper470 admits a complete finite exception using rank two before rank seven.\n\n**Status: finite construction and scoped negative result. No new kappa or selected supplier adoption.**\n\n- Keep D, A, retained copies, scatter and the original B unchanged. Insert three gates after scatter, replace one cleanup donor and omit one cleanup gate. Every one of the 661 symbolic input columns is correct in both scalar directions.\n- Helper470's frame dimensions change from `0 -> 1 -> 8` to `0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 7`. The other 660 frame itineraries are identical. Complete ADDs are 24,305 -> 24,307, MOVEs 2,911 -> 2,912, and paid local rank mass 5,129 -> 5,128; all nine COPY/ERASE pairs remain.\n- Give exact target-access witnesses for all six single-rank-seven retirement failures, the five least-frame failures, and the working lower-frame exception. This does not exclude lower-frame preparation, later target-read cuts or other interfaces.\n- Price the explicit two-slot relocation relaxation with all returned/consumed idle rank. It is favorable at the pinned bit exponent, but no physical window assignment or new bit endpoint is claimed.\n\nAli Romman's [PR1043](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1043) already deletes helper470 through an earlier source-boundary change and includes a hosted invoice. This does not improve that result or combine its savings. The distinct evidence is the unchanged-prefix endpoint and the six-candidate restoration classification. [PR1128](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1128)'s boundary model, Hanson Sun's [PR1079](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1079) census, Sagar Thakrar's [PR1023](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1023) hosting incentive, and DreamingOfClouds/eumemic's PR589/555 lineage are credited. [PR1179](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1179)'s kernel entrance is a separate mechanism.\n\nCatalogue card `bit-helper-contract`: **scope changed** from the card's H2/K repair to an H4/terminal-frame investigation, after overlap with [PR1194](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1194). The donor's bit-supplier assignment is retained. [Task card and exact dependency pins](https://github.com/RossRichardson/integer-mult-bounds/blob/2a6d342645ba919392c121f94f3345430afe0240/research/bit-early-retirement-cut/TASK.json) record the reason and bounded domain.\n\nExact research base: `49b3157d1d89adcef16df8be98445451672be5ba`; submission refresh: `dadfea6e8a78ff6ba901705f87532a71c6f5bbb8`, with identical input and the same selected PR1094. The sole live input has Git/SHA256 pins; external predecessor heads and historical context are in SOURCES.json. Seed8, bit-supplier track. Only `research/bit-early-retirement-cut/` is added.\n\n[Proof, literal patch, certificate, scope and next steps](https://github.com/RossRichardson/integer-mult-bounds/blob/2a6d342645ba919392c121f94f3345430afe0240/research/bit-early-retirement-cut/README.md).\n\nReproduce from the repository root:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/bit-early-retirement-cut\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/bit-early-retirement-cut outcome=completed`.\n\nLocal validation passed: registered Python3.12 replay; both checkers and eleven test groups on Python3.9.6; byte-identical receipt regeneration on Python3.14.6; selected-record integrity and all five selected-result tests; whitespace and source-pin checks. The two implementations use packed rows/Fraction geometry and set rows/fraction-free integer geometry. Tests include 22 star omissions, three retirement omissions, both cleanup errors, frame faults, source/receipt corruptions and read-only offline relocation. Hosted CI is separate; no hosted pass is claimed.\n\nUnresolved: changed H4 cleanup admission, native 5/9/11-stage replay, actual owner/window assignment, packed precision/tape and outer/all-size obligations. The current complex supplier remains limiting. No full make verify, selected cold replay, or Lean theorem proof was run. Upstream and the selected frontier are untouched.\n\nSmallest useful follow-up: test helper470's `0,79,186,513` path against one actual rank-seven idle window and the H4 cleanup contract before pricing a supplier. This is blocked by native/physical admission, not by the finite scalar identity. The README and task card also identify the exact later-target-read cuts for the remaining candidates.\n\nPrepared by Ross Richardson with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in reasoning, both implementations, tests and writing; Apache-2.0. Separate code paths do not imply independent human review.\n",
